    <DataNode elementId="CPD-520" textLabel="quercetin" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="REFJWTPEDVJJIY-UHFFFAOYSA-M" dataSource="InChIKey" />
      <Graphics centerX="917.6902465820312" centerY="1550.0" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="xue, PMN, nilo-poyanco, SRI, caspi">Quercetin is a plant flavonol that is found in many fruits, vegetables, leaves, seeds, and grains. It was first isolated from an oak tree (genus |FRAME: TAX-3511|) hence its name. Quercetin has a bitter flavor and is used as an ingredient in dietary supplements, beverages, and foods. It is one of the most abundant dietary flavonoids. The compound was shown to act as a competitive inhibitor of |FRAME: EC-4.2.1.59| (FabZ) from the pathogenic bacterium |FRAME: TAX-210| |CITS: [18780820]|.</Comment>
